    "expectedRule": "Temporal Observatory tracks two calibration anchors. Clearing past_calibration_anchor sets law.pastCalibrated=true; clearing future_calibration_anchor sets law.futureCalibrated=true; both start false on entry. The law display '时间校准' shows 0/2 时序漂移 (danger), 1/2 单锚锁定 (warning), 2/2 双锚同步 (resolved, targetReached). While the past anchor is uncalibrated, encounters gain +20% defense; while the future anchor is uncalibrated, traps gain +20% damage and +20% dc; the boss gains +10% all stats per missing anchor (capped at 20%). Route gates: temporal_past_shortcut (past_shortcut_foyer to erased_patrol) opens with past_calibrated; temporal_future_shortcut (future_shortcut_foyer to accelerated_patrol) opens with future_calibrated; temporal_calibration_bridge (calibration_bridge to zero_hour_regent), temporal_boss_south_lock and temporal_east_time_lock open only with dual_calibrated. Closed gates expose their real block reasons and remove the edge from legal adjacent targets, so run/move through a closed gate is rejected illegal-move. Anchor calibration persists through a save-codec round-trip. Re-selecting a cleared anchor node is rejected already-resolved without changing law state or HP. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
